<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Wissembourg</h1><p class="st-meta">1306 CE – 1679 CE (approx.) · capital Wissembourg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A northern Alsatian imperial city that grew around a powerful Benedictine abbey and joined the Decapolis before passing to France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Wissembourg grew around the Benedictine abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wissembourg-abbey">Saints Peter and Paul</a>, founded in the 7th century on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lauter-rhine">Lauter</a>, where the monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otfrid-of-weissenburg">Otfrid</a> wrote his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-high-german">Old High German</a> Gospel Harmony in the 9th century. The townspeople slowly freed themselves from the abbot's lordship, and by the early 14th century the town ranked as a free imperial city. In 1354 it was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/decapolis">Decapolis</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guilds</a> governed the town, which lived from wine, crafts and the road between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-strasbourg">Strasbourg</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/electoral-palatinate">Palatinate</a>. The abbey remained a rival authority; it became a provostry in 1524 and was united with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-speyer">Prince-Bishopric of Speyer</a> in 1546. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> won a following among the townspeople, while the abbey stayed Catholic.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Repeatedly fought over in the 17th century, Wissembourg came under French protection after 1648, and annexation by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a> was confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-nijmegen">Treaty of Nijmegen</a> in 1679. The exiled Polish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski">Stanisław Leszczyński</a> later lived there. It is now a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bas-rhin">Bas-Rhin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1306 CE – 1679 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.69%;width:7.42%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1306 CE – 1679 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wissembourg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alsatian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Wissembourg, Weißenburg im Elsass</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-wissembourg" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Wissembourg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4863 466 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Wissembourg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5183 722L5918 1245M5183 722L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5918 1245h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5183 722h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5183 722h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Wissembourg. <a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-w